  "body": "In https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-fieldset-element\r\n> The name of the group is given by the first legend element that is a child of the fieldset element, if any. The remainder of the descendants form the group.\r\n\r\nI wasn't able to find another use of “name” in the sense that it is defined here, that is, I couldn't find any reference to how such a name would be used.\r\n\r\nThe term seems to be causing some confusion in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/1584 so this is a request for some clarification, and/or perhaps calling it the “legend or label”of the group (or “caption”, to be consistent with how `<label>` is defined) so it's at least clearly not the same as the name of the `<fieldset>` element.\r\n\r\n> The name attribute represents the element's name.",
